atchdog (1 sola memoria USB):**\n   * Como tu memoria `KINGSTON` (donde está `super.img`) está puesta ahorita en la caja para provocar el salto con `factory_update_param.aml`, el programa **primero atrapa la caja en Fastboot y apaga el Watchdog de 14 segundos** (dejándola congelada en Fastboot sin reiniciarse), y **luego te avisa para que pases la memoria USB de la caja a tu PC** y pueda flashear `super.img` completo conservando Widevine L1 y MAC.","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe previous change permanently blocks mentioning the \"Configuration → Compilation\" step due to ZTE's RSA-2048 encryption, which requires external programs or a specific token bypass. A new program was rewritten and executed in the foreground.\n\n\nThe program monitors four external channels every 250ms, each corresponding to a different boot mode triggered by external events or selections. Upon detecting a specific Product ID (PID) or Vendor ID (VID) signaling a particular boot mode, the program executes a set of commands to disable watchdogs, unlock bootloaders, and transition the device into fastboot or similar states, enabling direct flashing or image injection. These states are designed to bypass specific device locks.\n\n\n"}
